  {
    "id": "b91dfd63985dc770162778bb994e866941ca1f14ff0fc0bf18600ddd46e0ca86",
    "date": "2026-01-24T23:03:04.000Z",
    "author": "Gabe Rodriguez",
    "message": "Day 5 in the books 🌃. It’s finally feeling like our little family is falling into a rhythm. A few highlights in the last few days:\n\n- Clement is “cluster feeding”. He’ll spend hours at a time eating w/ momma and finds so much comfort just being near her. With me, he has a ~2hr expiration before he demands momma back (I’ll have to think of some techniques to win back his favor later). His weight is also quite good! He needed to gain 200g within two weeks and after a few days, he’s more than halfway there.\n\n- Breast feeding was a little tough to start with because Clement had a tongue tie which limited how well he could move his tongue. After a trip to the dentist and a tiny snip under the tongue, his latching has greatly improved. At the office, he got a little crowd oohing and aahing: “Wow, look how big he is, bellissimo!”\n\n- The food menu at the house has been top ⭐. Alexandra froze portions of our favorites of the last month that we are digging our way through (Alexandra’s vegetarian bolognese is out of this world). Also, friends have been dropping off soups, desserts, and home cooked meals. Tonight we had an amazing spicy curry from our british/asian friend.\n\n- We mentioned before that Clement only wants to sleep skin-on-skin. But we managed to find he will sleep in the portable bassinet if lined with alpaca fur and if he’s wearing german wool and a swedish onesie—this boy is starting to get some exotic preferences already 😅. Also, thanks Aunt Nuccia for the swaddle+side lay pro tip.\n\nThank you all for the love from afar, he’s feeling it 💜"
  },
